GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_CutoverStrategy> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_CutoverStrategy> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#CutoverStrategy> ;
    narr:childCount "21"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "e3c75c2df1a4d6b8ce07850fdf733affe72074b3" ;
    narr:narration """This hub holds a working session opened under [steering-group pressure to decide the shape now](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_1), resolving into a cutover doctrine: [a sequential one-site-at-a-time commitment, no parallel cutovers even for the small sites](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8), defended as [contained pain with a named owner versus unbounded concurrent risk](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13), and [summed as one at a time, with a soak](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_16). Two isolation rules qualify the sequencing: [reporting reads barred from the live system during cutover windows](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_26), ratified as [a runbook rule rather than negotiable guidance](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_31), and [vendor-held reference data persisting until the final site goes green](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_36). The session closes with [a read-back of the full position for the steering group](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_42). The reasoning generalizes into [bounded-friction-over-unbounded-risk](narr:Narrative_ContainedPainOverUnboundedRisk), [single-source-of-truth retention](narr:Narrative_SingleSourceOfTruthUntilFinalCutover), and [strict workload isolation](narr:Narrative_StrictWorkloadIsolationDuringCutover). Newer attachments extend the span well beyond the session: [retention mandates and extraction scoping sequenced ahead of vendor decommissioning agreements](narr:Position_DecommissioningRetentionSequencing), [preservation of closed legacy records in self-describing open archives](narr:Position_LegacyRecordArchivalStrategy), [an unvoiced question about cross-site operational learning and skill compounding](narr:Position_CrossSiteOperationalLearning), [separation of cutover gate-approval rights from schedule incentives](narr:Position_CutoverGatekeeperRoleSeparation), [definition and testing of pre-cutover source data quality thresholds](narr:Position_PreCutoverDataQualityGateEnforcement), and [how unresolved programme vulnerabilities are presented to oversight bodies](narr:Position_ProactiveGovernanceRiskDisclosure) — the last three carrying no voiced claim yet, standing as open frames alongside the settled doctrine.""" ;
    narr:reaction """Nothing moved for this hub: the newer attachments extend the thematic span beyond the session into decommissioning sequencing, archival strategy, and three still-unvoiced open frames, but the settled cutover doctrine and its two isolation rules read exactly as before, so the prior narration holds.""" ;
